<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Msauli H1 income losses deepen.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Msauli H1 income losses deepen.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    4.32 loss   vs     3.56 loss</p>
<p>    Interest received	1.30	  vs     1.12</p>
<p>    Turnover		  26.49	  vs     37.35</p>
<p>    Rationalisation costs  5.94	  vs     1.32</p>
<p>Full name: Msauli Asbes Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had decided not to maintain these production levels due to lower sales volumes and stock build-up.</p>
<p>The firm said it decided to implement a major rationalisation programme to bring production and sales volumes in line and had made a provision of 5.25 million rand in the interim results.</p>
<p>The firm added that due to the restructuring process dividend prospects were &quot;remote&quot;.</p>
